From e8d9f6bc54a625405850f74db1cedbd9d77b4692 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:02:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] perf(tui): gate notice polls on claimable content,
 not every board commit

The hub's tui-notif-poller threads used 11% of a core (10% of serve samples in
_notif_poll_kanban) with nothing to deliver (t_01a1cee98b798343).

Root cause: each chat's poller gated every board on PRAGMA data_version, and the
main board commits ~40 times a minute with heartbeats, claims and run stamps that
no poller reads. The gate opened on nearly every 5 s tick, so every live chat ran
a full writable claim poll of every board. The remote half re-read and re-wrote
the whole observation ledger (one SELECT per terminal card under BEGIN
IMMEDIATE) on every replica commit, which a remote heartbeat also triggers.

- notification_idle.board_signature: what a chat's poll could claim, i.e. the
  newest deliverable-kind event id (AUTOINCREMENT, scanned incrementally) and the
  chat's own tui subscription rows (cursor, in-flight mark). It is read once per
  commit for every chat in the process. Bookkeeping commits and other chats'
  subscription changes keep it. A table-less file still keys on data_version,
  and an unreadable one is never unchanged. The quiet-board memo, the post-poll
  board_quiet proof and the in-flight liveness retries are unchanged.
- kanban_remote_observations._persist: observation rows are insert-once, so
  first_seen is remembered per ledger file. A replica commit with no new
  terminal state opens no ledger. Freshness values are identical, and a
  restarted backend reads the same rows back.
- _session_lineage: reuse a found chain for 30 s instead of opening state.db
  per chat per tick. A chat not yet in the store is looked up again.

Synthetic bench (9 chats, 1600 tui subs, heartbeat-only commit per tick):
local 24.1 -> 4.4 ms CPU/tick and 270 -> 0 full polls; remote collect opens
the ledger 30 -> 0 times.
